## What to do
Create the setup script that registers the 4 quality-tier label definitions on the Bluesky labeler account. This is run once during initial setup.

### Implementation
```typescript
// Run with: npx tsx src/labeler/set-labels.ts

import { BSKY_IDENTIFIER, BSKY_PASSWORD, DID } from "../lib/config"
import { LABELS } from "../lib/constants"

// Use @skyware/labeler/scripts to push label definitions
// Same pattern as labeler-starter-kit-bsky/src/set-labels.ts

async function main() {
  if (!BSKY_IDENTIFIER || !BSKY_PASSWORD) {
    console.error("Error: BSKY_IDENTIFIER and BSKY_PASSWORD must be set in .env")
    process.exit(1)
  }

  if (!DID) {
    console.error("Error: DID must be set in .env")
    process.exit(1)
  }

  console.log(`Setting up labels for ${DID}...`)
  console.log(`Using account: ${BSKY_IDENTIFIER}`)

  // Login and set label definitions
  // Map LABELS to the format expected by @skyware/labeler:
  //   { identifier, severity: "inform", blurs: "none", defaultSetting: "warn", adultOnly: false, locales: [...] }

  // Call setLabelerLabelDefinitions() from @skyware/labeler/scripts
  // OR use @atproto/api directly to declareLabelDefs if @skyware/labeler/scripts is not available

  // If using @skyware/labeler/scripts pattern:
  // 1. Import { setLabelerLabelDefinitions } from "@skyware/labeler/scripts"
  // 2. Create login credentials object
  // 3. Call with DID, credentials, and label definitions
  // 4. Log success for each label

  // If @skyware/labeler/scripts is not importable, use @atproto/api:
  // 1. Create BskyAgent and login
  // 2. Call agent.com.atproto.repo.putRecord to update the labeler service record
  // 3. Include all 4 label definitions in the labelValues array

  for (const label of LABELS) {
    console.log(`  ✓ ${label.identifier}: ${label.locales[0]?.name}`)
  }

  console.log("Done! All labels registered.")
}

main().catch(err => {
  console.error("Failed to set labels:", err)
  process.exit(1)
})
```

### Label definitions format
Each label maps to:
- identifier: from LABELS[].identifier
- severity: "inform" (informational, not a content warning)
- blurs: "none" (no content blurring)
- defaultSetting: "warn" (shown by default with a note)
- adultOnly: false
- locales: from LABELS[].locales

